# UI Package Conventions

## File naming

- Use **lowercase with dashes** for all UI file names.
- Examples: `page-header.tsx`, `user-detail-modal.tsx`, `create-user-dialog.tsx`, `use-confirm.ts`
- Do not use: `PageHeader.tsx`, `UserDetailModal.tsx`, `useConfirm.ts` (PascalCase or camelCase in filenames).

## Components and organization

- **One component per file** when the component is non-trivial (more than a few lines or reused).
- **Extract small components** into their own files instead of defining them in the same file as the page or parent.
- **Use directories** to group related files:
  - `components/user/` for user-related components
  - `components/role/`, `components/tenant/`, `components/auth/`, etc.
  - `pages/` for page components
  - `hooks/` for custom hooks
- Keep each file focused: one main export (component or hook) per file; small helpers can stay in the same file if they are not reused.

## Props and formatting

- **Component props**: If a component receives **more than 2 props**, put **one prop per line**.
- **Arrays** (e.g. list of items, options): If **more than 2 elements**, put one element per line.
- **Objects** (e.g. `sx`, config, style): If **more than 2 keys**, put one key-value per line.

### Examples

**Props (more than 2 → one per line):**

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<PageHeader
  title="User Management"
  description="Manage users and roles"
  onRefresh={loadUsers}
  loading={loading}
  action={createButton}
/>

// ❌ BAD (3+ props on one line)
<PageHeader title="User Management" description="Manage users" onRefresh={loadUsers} loading={loading} />
```

**Arrays (more than 2 → one per line):**

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
const options = [
  { value: 'all', label: 'All' },
  { value: 'active', label: 'Active' },
  { value: 'inactive', label: 'Inactive' },
];
```

**Objects (more than 2 keys → one per line):**

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<Box
  sx={{
    display: 'flex',
    alignItems: 'center',
    gap: 2,
    p: 2,
  }}
/>
```

## Summary

| Rule | Do |
|------|-----|
| File names | `lowercase-with-dashes.tsx` |
| Components | One main component per file; extract small components to new files |
| Directories | Use folders to organize by feature (user, role, auth, etc.) |
| Props | 1 prop per line when there are more than 2 props |
| Arrays / objects | 1 item per line when there are more than 2 items |
